/-!
# Checked extension obstructions for both mixed tensor orientations

The displayed F₄ matrices are checked against the actual tensor models at
S, T, BSB and BTB under the published point-stabilizer equivalence. Every
packed equation row is checked against those matrices. Eighteen checked
row combinations force the first column to vanish in either orientation.

The discovery data is untrusted; every identity below is checked by the
Lean kernel. Field codes, coordinate conventions, regeneration instructions
and the existing ATLAS attribution are recorded in `Certificate/source/`.
Source context: Guralnick–Malle I, Proposition 5.1, pp.15–16; the actual word
comparison and matrix attribution are in ExtensionExclusion/Relations.lean.
-/

